lessons.content:
### Decision Making in Java
Java uses standard structured control flow:
```java
if (score >= 90) {
    grade = 'A';
} else if (score >= 80) {
    grade = 'B';
} else {
    grade = 'C';
}
```

### Switch Statements in Java
Unlike C/C++, Java allows switching on:
- Primitive integers (`byte`, `short`, `int`, `char`)
- Enum types
- `String` objects (since Java 7)
- Wrapper classes (`Integer`, `Character`)

```java
switch (role) {
    case "ADMIN":
        grantFullAccess();
        break;
    case "USER":
        grantStandardAccess();
        break;
    default:
        denyAccess();
        break;
}
```

