### Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) in Java
Java is fundamentally built on the four pillars of OOP:
1. **Encapsulation**: Bundling state and behavior, restricting direct access to internal fields.
2. **Inheritance**: Deriving new classes from existing classes.
3. **Polymorphism**: Treating derived objects uniformly through a common interface.
4. **Abstraction**: Hiding complex internal implementation details.

### Designing a Class
```java
public class User {
    // 1. Private fields (encapsulated)
    private String username;
    private int score;

    // 2. Constructor
    public User(String username, int score) {
        this.username = username;
        this.score = score;
    }

    // 3. Public Getters & Setters
    public String getUsername() {
        return username;
    }
    public int getScore() {
        return score;
    }
}
```

